{
  "case_id": "2017-16-784",
  "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: So why should it matter whether the transmission was through the banks rather than handed over by Valley View to Merit?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Merit Management Group, LP",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "fraudulent. My argument is that the intermediate transfers can't be separated from the overall end-to-end transfer, and so that by avoiding the overall transfer, the trustee would necessarily be avoiding the intermediate transfers as well.\nTo think of it a different way -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: -- can you help me out with what happens to the law of preferences under your interpretation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Could I take you back to Justice Alito's question, perhaps just put a little bit of a different spin on it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I guess you're asking a court to make a shift in transfers in the middle of the analysis."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Well, I was just going to say the second point why they're not making it, which is it doesn't apply here anyways, which is, as I read that provision, it is very narrow, and it protects the customer only when the bank is acting -- when the bank is acting as an agent or custodian."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Could -- what if the trustee -- would there be situations in which it would make sense for the trustee to want to avoid one of the intermediary transfers rather than simply the ultimate one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0013",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: I don't think they -- I mean, they could try, but I don't think they would get away with it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Well, if we're -- if we're writing the -- the opinion to accept your proposition, how do we -- how do we qualify it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 0.97,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: What do you think is wrong, Mr. Clement, with the alternative approach? If I understand the alternative approach, which Justice Kennedy was referring to, it's more of a functional analysis; you ask who has dominion and control of a particular piece of property at a particular point."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: So -- but, Mr. Clement, on that, I assume your friend will get up and say, well, a lot of those charitable contributions are by check, and those aren't covered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Trustee's amicus brief",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "as the trustee's amicus brief said, to sort of carve out, you know, leveraged buyouts from the fraudulent avoidance laws, that's carving out a lot because these are transactions where there is a risk that's quite considerable to mulcting the interest of the unsecured creditors."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0003-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "both sides in the Tribune case have filed amicus briefs."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0003-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Gorsuch mentioned the Second Circuit's opinion, which is justifiably concerned about what happens, there are thousands of defendants in that case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0003-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if Goldman Sachs or Merrill Lynch received a distribution in that case for its own account, they don't have liability, that transfer can't be avoided."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Over the past 30 years, Congress has expanded and expanded and expanded the safe harbor to bolt on different concepts, including financial institutions."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "4b2f37aab100af1b8f1cb48a5ac44cf30ed247975d7250075504b283c4639e6e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-4b2f37aab100-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And if Congress thought that the courts were out of line, it could very well have cut the statute back. It didn't do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2017-16-784",
